From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: A733 minimal — add USB3 (dwc3 + COMB0 combo-PHY)

Wires the USB3.1 SuperSpeed path on the minimal A733 boot DT: the USB3 DRD
controller (@0x06A00000, xHCI 1.20 — Allwinner names this block "USB2" in the
CCU/IRQ tables), the SERDES subsystem clock/reset controller that gates it, the
COMB0 SERDES combo-PHY that carries its SuperSpeed lanes to Type-C J4, the
RTC-CCU that gates the SERDES DCXO, and the J4 VBUS switch.

- usb3@6a00000: "allwinner,sun60i-a733-dwc3", the flattened generic glue (no
  child node). It takes all five clocks and the controller reset and creates the
  core only once they are up. The earlier bare "snps,dwc3" shape could not do
  that: dwc3 enables only clocks it knows by name, and two of these five have no
  such name — the SERDES bus gates are not CCU clocks at all, and CLK_USB2_MF is
  required although its name fits no dwc3 slot (booting the same Image without
  it gives "soft reset failed / -ETIMEDOUT / -110", and so does dropping U2_REF
  and calling MF "ref"; SUSPEND was never removed on a boot, and the two SERDES
  gates have never been modelled as clocks on a boot at all). It also made the bring-up depend on the
  combo-PHY probing first, which stopped happening when the Type-C connector's
  graph closed a devlink ring. IRQ GIC_SPI 155 (INTID 187, UM source "USB2" —
  the controller IRQ, not the COMB0 USB3 event INTID
  217 = GIC_SPI 185; INTID 185 is PCIE0_MSI). reset RST_USB_2. phys = u2phy +
  combophy0. dr_mode host, super-speed-plus.
- serdes_ccu@6c00000: allwinner,sun60i-a733-serdes-ccu (patch `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-serdes-subsystem-clocks`), 16 bytes
  covering SUBSYS_PCIE_BGR (0x0004, not modelled yet) and SUBSYS_USB3P1_BGR
  (0x0008). Its two input clocks are the SERDES bus-matrix gates the CCU does
  have -- AHB 0x05C0 bit8 and MBUS 0x05E0 bit28, added
  to the CCU in `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-serdes-combophy-clock` -- so the tree reads AHB/MBUS -> matrix gate -> subsystem
  gate -> block, which is what the hardware is. It consumes RST_BUS_SERDES,
  without which its own registers read zero and swallow writes.
- combophy0@6c01000: allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy (patch `phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy`). Three
  windows ioremapped by index: link 0x06C01000, top2 0x06C06000, PMA
  0x06C80000. The SERDES subsystem page it used to map as window 0 belongs to
  serdes_ccu now, so the node moved to the address of its first remaining
  window. clocks serdes (main-CCU CLK_SERDES_PHY_CFG) + dcxo-serdes0 (RTC-CCU);
  reset RST_BUS_SERDES, shared with serdes_ccu; #phy-cells 0
  (of_phy_simple_xlate).
- u2phy@6b00000: gains resets = <&serdes_ccu RST_USB3_USB2PHY>. That bit was
  written from the combo-PHY's phy_init before, which is another device's
  driver.
- rtc_ccu@7090000: allwinner,sun60i-a733-rtc-ccu (patch `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-minimal-rtc-ccu`), parent r-ahb.
- reg_usb3_vbus: SGM2576 U2, enable USB0-DRVVBUS = PL2 (r_pio bank 0 pin 2),
  verified against the schematic.

usb3, combophy0 and u2phy ship status = "okay". They were disabled until an SS
link was proven on iron, on the grounds that a half-probe could disturb the
shared COMB0/DP power domain. That condition is met: 2026-07-21 on the 8 GiB board the link
trains at 10 Gbps in both plug orientations.

The J4 VBUS regulator is deliberately NOT regulator-always-on. Its enable is a
GPIO (PL2 = USB0-DRVVBUS on the SGM2576 U2) precisely so the Type-C port
controller can gate it, and TCPM needs that control: SRC_ATTACH_WAIT only
advances to SRC_ATTACHED when `tcpm_port_is_source(port) && port->vbus_vsafe0v`
(tcpm.c), i.e. VBUS must be off before a source port attaches -- Rp is advertised
with VBUS down, the sink presents Rd, and only then does the source raise VBUS.
Holding VBUS on permanently kept the state machine in SRC_ATTACH_WAIT forever:
CC interrupts arrived on every plug (the TCPC irq counter moved 1 -> 3 across an
unplug/replug on the 8 GiB board, 2026-07-21) and no partner ever appeared.

Verified: dtc builds it with no new warning and the compiled dtb carries the
serdes_ccu node, the five clock phandles on usb3 and the reset on u2phy. NOT
verified here: the board.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -16,8 +16,11 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-r-ccu.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-rtc-ccu.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-serdes-ccu.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/reset/sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/reset/sun60i-a733-serdes-ccu.h>
 
 / {
 	model = "Radxa Cubie A7S (A733 minimal M1)";
@@ -514,6 +517,23 @@
 		regulator-always-on;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * VBUS for the Type-C J4 SuperSpeed port, switched by SGM2576 U2 whose
+	 * enable is USB0-DRVVBUS = PL2 (the "USB0" net name is a schematic label;
+	 * on page-12 it gates J4's VBUS switch).
+	 * PL2 = r_pio bank index 0 (PL), pin 2.
+	 * Deliberately NOT regulator-always-on: the HUSB311 owns this rail as its
+	 * vbus-supply, and TCPM only leaves SRC_ATTACH_WAIT with VBUS down.
+	 */
+	reg_usb3_vbus: regulator-usb3-vbus {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "usb3-vbus";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		gpio = <&r_pio 0 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+	};
+
 	memory@40000000 {
 		device_type = "memory";
 		/* Fallback 1 GiB; the bootloader fixes up the real size. */
@@ -1129,6 +1149,160 @@
 		};
 
 		/*
+		 * USB3.1 SuperSpeed: the USB3 DRD (Allwinner "USB2" block,
+		 * UM USB3P1_DRD @0x06A00000, xHCI 1.20) + the COMB0 SERDES combo-PHY
+		 * that carries the SuperSpeed lanes to Type-C J4.
+		 *
+		 * dwc3 is described flat, through the generic glue: the glue owns the
+		 * clocks and the reset and only then creates the core, so the
+		 * controller is never reached before its bus clocks run. The bare
+		 * snps,dwc3 shape this replaced could not express that -- two of the
+		 * five clocks have no dwc3 clock name to go by -- and it left the
+		 * bring-up depending on the combo-PHY probing first, which fw_devlink
+		 * stopped honouring once the Type-C connector closed a graph ring.
+		 *
+		 * IRQ = GIC_SPI 155 (INTID 187, UM source "USB2" -- the controller
+		 * IRQ, not the COMB0 USB3 event, which is INTID 217 = GIC_SPI 185.
+		 * The old note here said "IRQ 185" and mixed the two numbering
+		 * spaces: INTID 185 is PCIE0_MSI.
+		 */
+		usb3: usb@6a00000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-dwc3";
+			reg = <0x0 0x06a00000 0x0 0x10000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 155 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			/*
+			 * MF and U2_REF are each measured as required: booting
+			 * the same Image without either gives "soft reset
+			 * failed / -110" (the 8 GiB board, 2026-07-29). SUSPEND has never
+			 * been removed on a boot, and aclk/hclk -- gates in the
+			 * SERDES subsystem page, not in the CCU -- have never
+			 * existed as modelled clocks on a boot at all, so their
+			 * necessity here is reasoned, not measured. The first
+			 * board test of this node is what settles them.
+			 */
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_USB2_U2_REF>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_USB2_MF>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_USB2_SUSPEND>,
+				 <&serdes_ccu CLK_USB3_ACLK>,
+				 <&serdes_ccu CLK_USB3_HCLK>;
+			clock-names = "ref", "mf", "suspend", "aclk", "hclk";
+			/* Force the suspend clock to sys24M (mux bit24=1); POR is
+			 * osc32k (32 kHz). Feeds GCTL.PWRDNSCALE. */
+			assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_USB2_SUSPEND>;
+			assigned-clock-rates = <24000000>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_USB_2>;
+			phys = <&u2phy>, <&combophy0>;
+			phy-names = "usb2-phy", "usb3-phy";
+			dr_mode = "host";
+			maximum-speed = "super-speed-plus";
+			/*
+			 * Vendor dwc3 quirks: without the susphy quirks the core
+			 * soft-reset sends the PHYs to suspend and waits for an ack
+			 * that never comes -> DCTL.CSFTRST never clears -> -110.
+			 */
+			snps,dis_enblslpm_quirk;
+			snps,dis-u1-entry-quirk;
+			snps,dis-u2-entry-quirk;
+			snps,dis_u3_susphy_quirk;
+			snps,dis_u2_susphy_quirk;
+
+			/* Target for the connector's mandatory port@0 (HS). Inert:
+			 * dwc3 only builds a role switch when usb-role-switch is
+			 * present, and this port is host-only.
+			 */
+			status = "okay";
+
+			port {
+				usb3_hs: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&usb_con_hs>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+
+		/*
+		 * SERDES subsystem clock/reset controller (patch `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-serdes-subsystem-clocks`). Two registers:
+		 * the PCIe bus gates at 0x0004 (not modelled yet) and the USB3 ones at
+		 * 0x0008 -- bit17 AXI, bit16 AHB, bit4 the companion PHY's reset-n.
+		 * The whole page is dead while
+		 * RST_BUS_SERDES is asserted, so the controller consumes that reset
+		 * and holds it deasserted for everyone behind it.
+		 */
+		serdes_ccu: clock-controller@6c00000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-serdes-ccu";
+			reg = <0x0 0x06c00000 0x0 0x10>;
+			/*
+			 * The two bus-matrix gates that feed the whole SERDES
+			 * block: AHB 0x05C0 bit8 and
+			 * MBUS 0x05E0 bit28. They are the upstream of the
+			 * per-device gates in this page.
+			 */
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_SERDES>, <&ccu CLK_MBUS_SERDES>;
+			clock-names = "ahb", "mbus";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_SERDES>;
+			#clock-cells = <1>;
+			#reset-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
+		/*
+		 * COMB0 SERDES combo-PHY (allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy, patch
+		 * `phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy`). Three windows the driver ioremaps by index: 0 = link
+		 * @0x06C01000 (LINK_CTRL0-3 + LINK_STUS), 1 = SERDES top2 @0x06C06000
+		 * (PIPE-clk mux + DP raw-serdes conv), 2 = PMA @0x06C80000 (0xC008
+		 * reset-path nudge). The SERDES subsystem page at 0x06C00000 is NOT
+		 * one of them -- it is the serdes_ccu's, above. serdes-phy-cfg =
+		 * 100 MHz config clock (main CCU); dcxo-serdes0 = RTC-CCU DCXO gate.
+		 * #phy-cells = 0 (of_phy_simple_xlate). vbus is on reg_usb3_vbus.
+		 */
+		combophy0: phy@6c01000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy";
+			reg = <0x0 0x06c01000 0x0 0x1000>,
+			      <0x0 0x06c06000 0x0 0x1000>,
+			      <0x0 0x06c80000 0x0 0x20000>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_SERDES_PHY_CFG>,
+				 <&rtc_ccu CLK_RTC_DCXO_SERDES0>;
+			clock-names = "serdes", "dcxo-serdes0";
+			/* shared: the serdes_ccu holds it deasserted too */
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_SERDES>;
+			#phy-cells = <0>;
+
+			/* The SS lane mux lives inside COMB0 -- there is no
+			 * external mux and no select GPIO on this board
+			 * at all. So the PHY itself is
+			 * the Type-C orientation switch, and TCPM reaches it
+			 * through the graph below. The property must sit on this
+			 * node: the framework matches the endpoint's remote
+			 * *device* parent.
+			 */
+			orientation-switch;
+
+			status = "okay";
+
+			port {
+				combophy0_ss: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&usb_con_ss>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+
+		/*
+		 * USB2.0 UTMI companion PHY for the USB3 DRD (net USB2-U2). The dwc3
+		 * core soft-reset needs this out of power-down. Driver = patch `phy-allwinner-a733-add-usb2-companion-phy`
+		 * (clk res-dcap, Rext RESCAL via res_base, VBUSVLDEXT + clear SIDDQ).
+		 * Its reset-n is bit4 of the SERDES subsystem's USB3 gate register, so
+		 * it comes from the serdes_ccu rather than from this block.
+		 */
+		u2phy: phy@6b00000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb2-phy";
+			reg = <0x0 0x06b00000 0x0 0x800>,   /* u2_base */
+			      <0x0 0x03000000 0x0 0x300>;   /* SYSCFG res_base (Rext) */
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_RES_DCAP_24M>;
+			clock-names = "res_dcap";
+			resets = <&serdes_ccu RST_USB3_USB2PHY>;
+			#phy-cells = <0>;
+			status = "okay";
+		};
+
+		/*
 		 * AON / CPUS domain. The R-CCU (PRCM @0x07010000) provides the AON
 		 * bus clocks; the r_pio (S_GPIO @0x07025000) is the AON pin bank
 		 * PL/PM. Base + geometry from the pin tables of the A733 user manual (PL @0x00/14 pins, PM @0x30/
@@ -1181,5 +1355,18 @@
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * RTC-CCU (PRCM @0x07090000, AON domain). Provides the two SERDES
+		 * DCXO gates (XO_CTRL1 @0x16c bit4/5); the COMB0 combo-PHY consumes
+		 * dcxo-serdes0. Parent = r-ahb (from the R-CCU). Driver = patch `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-minimal-rtc-ccu`.
+		 */
+		rtc_ccu: clock-controller@7090000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-rtc-ccu";
+			reg = <0x0 0x07090000 0x0 0x400>;
+			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_R_AHB>;
+			clock-names = "r-ahb";
+			#clock-cells = <1>;
+		};
 	};
 };
